<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Video library (Duotone). Mockup: DuotoneWall.dc.html (view 500). Includes: Includes_Views_Video.xml.
	Kodi id contract (Estuary Omega MyVideoNav.xml): <views> 500 Wall (movies, sets, shows, seasons,
	music videos) / 503 Episodes (episodes, seasons) / 50 List (everything); 0.9.16: 505 Poster, 506 Screens; 0.9.18: 510 Rows (films, sets, series, music videos; last = never a default)
	(everything), 507 Sheet (poster content) in Includes_Views_More.xml (_src/make_views_more.py). Defaults by
	viewtype: list -> 503 for episodes / seasons, 50 otherwise; the new views' types are never asked for. menucontrol 9000 (header filter bar, 9321-9326); 3 sort-by / 4 sort-order
	(hidden buttons the bar clicks); 14 watched toggle (SendClick only). 63 = scrollbar of 503.
	Colour: Films vermilion; tvshows / seasons / episodes cobalt ($VAR[SectionColor], DT_SecSeries).

	Focus map: header bar 9000 Down -> view. View Up (top row) -> header bar. Back = parent folder;
	Back on the bar returns to the view.
-->
<window>
	<defaultcontrol always="true">50</defaultcontrol>
	<menucontrol>9000</menucontrol>
	<backgroundcolor>ground_static</backgroundcolor>
	<views>500,503,505,506,507,50,510</views>
	<!-- empty folder: Kodi can't focus an empty view, so land on the header bar instead -->
	<onload condition="Integer.IsEqual(Container.NumItems,0) + !Container.IsUpdating">SetFocus(9000)</onload>
	<include>Anim_WindowOpenClose</include>
	<controls>
		<include>VidView_Window</include>
	</controls>
</window>
